{{!
    Upstream's template, with the non-scalar attributes made to work.

    It declares an object as a string and a list as a ListAttribute, and then
    converts neither -- the field reaches the schema and the model struct and
    is silently never sent or read. Here anything that is not a scalar is a
    JSON string: jsontypes.Normalized so that a re-ordered object coming back
    from the server is not a permanent diff, and json.Marshal/Unmarshal either
    side of the wire.
